secubox-toolbox (2.3.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Fix (#498) : NetworkManager connection `id` was the raw User-Agent
    string ("Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:151.0)...") which
    looks awful in the Network panel. Use `village3b-r3-<last-octet>`
    instead — short, stable, distinct per peer.
  * lxc-provision (#498) : substantial improvements toward the
    eventual wg LXC cutover :
      - Use lxc-create --template download (works for unprivileged ;
        `debian` template needs privileged-only).
      - Replace the LXC's live config at /data/lxc/<name>/config
        (LXC ignores /etc/lxc/<name>.conf for the actual runtime
        config).
      - Push runtime IP + systemd-networkd profile + working DNS
        via lxc-attach (unprivileged containers can't self-assign
        a static IP via lxc.net.0.ipv4.address).
      - Install python3 inside the container post-network so apt
        actually resolves names.
    Known roadblock NOT yet resolved : the wg LXC bind mount of
    /etc/secubox/toolbox/ca-wg fails because the host dir is
    0750 root:secubox-toolbox — invisible to the unprivileged LXC's
    mapped UID. Operator must either chmod the CA cert dir to 0755
    OR drop lxc.idmap from the config to switch to privileged mode
    (matches the existing mitmproxy LXC). Documented inline in the
    LXC template. Cutover stays opt-in until this is resolved.

